<measure n="41"><staff n="1"><layer n="1"><note xml:id="n120_1" dur="2" pname="d" oct="4"/><note xml:id="n121" dur="4" pname="c" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl wordpos="t">tion</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="n122" dur="4" pname="d" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>and</syl></verse></note></layer></staff></measure>
<measure n="42"><staff n="1"><layer n="1"><note xml:id="n123" dur="2" pname="e" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl wordpos="i" con="d">mu</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="n124" dur="4" pname="d" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl wordpos="t">tual</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="n125" dur="4" pname="c" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl eol="1">rest</syl></verse></note></layer></staff><harm staff="1" place="above" tstamp="1">C</harm><tie startid="#n125" endid="#n126"/></measure>
<measure n="43" right="end"><staff n="1"><layer n="1"><note xml:id="n126" dur="1" pname="c" oct="4"/></layer></staff></measure>
</section>
</score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>But Lord through my attainments, my introspective self</l><l>Arises as excluding wall to build</l><l>I long for my perfection, my little foxes loose.</l><l>Lord free me from the self, fulfill Your plan.</l><l>Take me to the cross</l><l>In the rough clefts of the rock I would remain</l><l>By Your resurrection pow&#x27;r empowers me</l><l>And encourage me to rise and come away,</l></lg>
<lg label="Chorus"><l>Then I&#x27;m conformed (in union, I&#x27;m</l><l>To the death of Christ Your bed, palanquin,</l><l>Experience espoused to be</l><l>Resurrection life one with Solomon)</l><l>Move with God,</l><l>As a steady pillar of smoke, like God!</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Continue, Lord, to call me that I would be in You</l><l>To live in Your ascension, high above.</l><l>As God&#x27;s new creation in resurrection that</l><l>My Christ in many aspects I&#x27;ll enjoy.</l><l>Looking from the top of Amana, Senir, Hermon</l><l>While we fight the enemy</l><l>Enjoy Christ in His death, resurrection and ascension, Spirit, too.</l></lg>
<lg label="Chorus"><l>I then become (with a spring shut up</l><l>A rich garden, full and with fountain sealed)</l><l>Of choicest fruits, (the north wind wakes,</l><l>And chief spices flow and the south wind blows)</l><l>Exuding Christ —</l><l>Fragrant garden for the Triune God</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>A sanctuary — Tirzah, Jerusalem its guard</l><l>Still has a separating veil, the flesh.</l><l>So deeper still You call me to live within the veil</l><l>That stronger cross I would experience now.</l><l>For Your grace to me is sufficient, it supplies abundantly</l><l>To enter into the Holiest place of all</l><l>Hidden manna, budding rod and inner law</l></lg>
<lg label="Chorus"><l>I then become (so spiritual,</l><l>Heaven&#x27;s moon and sun and so heavenly)</l><l>God&#x27;s army — fight (we terrify</l><l>Overcome as one; our enemy.)</l><l>The Shulammite,</l><l>As the ultimate, New Jerusalem</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>